WEBVTT

00:00.067 --> 00:03.969
Episode 21
Current

00:31.531 --> 00:32.657
Satsuki!

00:35.302 --> 00:38.271
I'm sorry to have made you wait.

00:38.338 --> 00:41.364
No, I just got here early.

00:41.441 --> 00:42.601
You're right.

00:42.676 --> 00:43.973
It's still 10 minutes early.

00:46.613 --> 00:48.877
Oh, this?

00:48.949 --> 00:51.417
I got this at the arcade the other day...

00:52.452 --> 00:54.852
I guess it doesn't suit me, does it?

00:54.921 --> 00:55.979
Here.

00:56.056 --> 00:58.388
If you fancy it, I'll give it to you.

01:02.229 --> 01:03.992
But...

01:04.064 --> 01:05.827
It's rather peaceful.

01:05.899 --> 01:08.891
But this Tokyo will soon fall to ruins.

01:09.936 --> 01:13.167
When Tokyo falls, the Earth will also fall to ruins.

01:14.207 --> 01:19.668
And most of the organisms that live on Earth will perish.

01:20.781 --> 01:22.646
That's a scary story.

01:24.017 --> 01:28.147
Do you have someone that will be sad for you, Yuto?

01:29.890 --> 01:34.156
Back when we talked about why we can't kill humans...

01:34.227 --> 01:36.092
...you mentioned it.

01:36.163 --> 01:39.360
That people would
be sad because of it.

01:39.433 --> 01:41.162
Oh?

01:41.234 --> 01:43.327
Did I say such a thing?

01:43.403 --> 01:44.370
Yes.

01:44.438 --> 01:45.803
Did I?

01:52.145 --> 01:54.909
You seem to be well-liked by water.

01:54.981 --> 01:56.972
Yes, for some reason.

01:59.586 --> 02:03.682
Yuto, why did you go along with Kanoe's invitation?

02:03.757 --> 02:06.749
Is there something you want to have or do?

02:06.827 --> 02:08.454
Not at all.

02:08.528 --> 02:11.429
It's good to fight against destiny...

02:11.498 --> 02:13.796
But I thought it'd also be interesting...

02:13.867 --> 02:17.860
...to go along with the flow and see how things end.

02:17.938 --> 02:19.963
Is that too vague an answer?

02:24.010 --> 02:25.238
Well, let's go.

02:26.279 --> 02:28.440
You don't mind Italian food, right?

03:10.390 --> 03:14.258
He's been like that ever since Arashi disappeared.

03:16.830 --> 03:18.923
Let's leave him alone for now.

03:18.999 --> 03:23.595
But Arashi liked Sorata so much...

03:23.670 --> 03:25.137
Why?

03:25.205 --> 03:27.036
Even though we don't know now...

03:27.107 --> 03:31.567
...I'm sure she did this because she had her own thoughts.

03:31.645 --> 03:33.579
Now cheer up.

03:33.647 --> 03:37.674
If you guys are depressed, Sorata will be in more pain, right?

03:37.751 --> 03:38.718
Yes...

03:39.786 --> 03:41.048
You're all right, too?

03:42.722 --> 03:45.020
He always supported me.

03:46.059 --> 03:49.756
So this time, I have to support him.

03:49.829 --> 03:50.887
That's true.

03:52.599 --> 03:55.625
I'm worried about those kids...

03:55.702 --> 03:56.896
Yes...

03:56.970 --> 03:59.370
The reason why Arashi disappeared...

03:59.439 --> 04:01.134
Do you understand why?

04:02.309 --> 04:03.571
Not really...

04:04.611 --> 04:05.578
But perhaps...

04:06.613 --> 04:07.637
Perhaps?

04:08.682 --> 04:11.310
Those two had feelings for each other.

04:12.352 --> 04:16.379
Perhaps disappearing from Sorata's life...

04:16.456 --> 04:19.016
...was one of her ways of loving him.

04:20.060 --> 04:21.493
Why is that so?

04:21.561 --> 04:22.858
I just have a hunch.

04:23.897 --> 04:27.060
The same can be said for you, right, Mr. Aoki?

04:27.133 --> 04:31.467
To keep your wife and daughter from being caught in this battle...

04:31.538 --> 04:33.733
...you reluctantly filed for divorce.

04:33.807 --> 04:36.571
And your wife doesn't know the true reason, either.

04:38.178 --> 04:39.270
That's true...

04:40.380 --> 04:44.783
I'm jealous that you can feel that much for one another...

04:44.851 --> 04:46.443
Oh, I'm sorry.

04:46.519 --> 04:48.419
This must be hard on you...

04:48.488 --> 04:50.149
No, it's all right.

04:50.223 --> 04:53.659
In any case, what we have to worry about is the youngsters.

04:53.727 --> 04:56.491
They're still very young, after all.

04:56.563 --> 05:00.055
Besides, it might take quite a bit more time...

05:00.133 --> 05:02.897
...before Kamui's true power awakens.

05:02.969 --> 05:05.563
We have to do something...

05:05.639 --> 05:06.606
Yes.

05:07.974 --> 05:09.532
Karen!

05:12.212 --> 05:15.181
Don't worry, I won't be reckless anymore.

05:15.248 --> 05:16.215
All right.

05:32.132 --> 05:34.191
That hurts, Beast...

05:36.770 --> 05:37.828
What's wrong?

05:39.506 --> 05:40.473
Beast...

05:40.540 --> 05:41.529
What is it?

05:41.608 --> 05:42.905
Let go of me...

05:50.950 --> 05:54.078
It looks like Beast isn't too happy today.

05:54.154 --> 05:55.382
Not happy?

05:55.455 --> 05:57.787
As if it's jealous of Yuto.

05:59.092 --> 06:00.957
At least, that's how it looks.

06:02.028 --> 06:05.896
But a computer would never have feelings or mood swings.

06:07.133 --> 06:08.566
Kanoe...

06:08.635 --> 06:09.863
What about you?

06:09.936 --> 06:11.733
Let's see...

06:11.805 --> 06:14.933
I'm fine as long as you're not bored.

06:15.008 --> 06:17.101
Yuto is a fun person.

06:17.177 --> 06:19.737
He hasn't changed one bit in all this time.

06:19.813 --> 06:23.874
Oh, do you want to hear about when I first met him?

06:23.950 --> 06:24.917
Yes.

06:25.952 --> 06:28.887
I knew of his face from quite a while back...

06:28.955 --> 06:32.322
...because I had seen him in my sister Hinoto's dreams.

06:32.392 --> 06:33.654
Both Yuto and you.

06:34.694 --> 06:37.925
But seeing him in person came much, much later.

06:37.997 --> 06:39.157
Above here...

06:44.204 --> 06:45.762
I knew at first glance.

06:53.880 --> 06:54.847
Hello.

07:09.062 --> 07:10.427
Is something the matter?

07:14.300 --> 07:15.733
Oh, brother...

07:15.802 --> 07:19.670
They'll get mad at me again if I don't go back to the office soon...

07:19.739 --> 07:21.798
You're the one I saw in the dreams.

07:21.875 --> 07:22.842
Dreams?

07:22.909 --> 07:24.206
Yes.

07:24.277 --> 07:27.610
Don't you have some sort of special power?

07:27.680 --> 07:29.545
Oh? Perhaps you mean...

07:36.723 --> 07:37.712
...this?

07:38.758 --> 07:40.419
A Dragon of Earth.

07:40.493 --> 07:41.892
A watermaster.

07:41.961 --> 07:44.429
Oh, they had such a name for this?

07:46.032 --> 07:48.125
Do you want to see more?

07:48.201 --> 07:50.260
You'll show me more from now on.

07:50.336 --> 07:52.770
Fine, I have no problems with that.

07:55.175 --> 07:57.200
It's like Yuto to say that.

07:57.277 --> 07:58.266
True.

07:58.344 --> 08:00.710
Not attaching himself to anything...

08:00.780 --> 08:02.873
Going with the flow...

08:02.949 --> 08:06.908
Satsuki, I thought you also hated being attached to something?

08:28.775 --> 08:31.300
A grain of wheat falls to the ground...

08:32.345 --> 08:34.142
...and bears much fruit.

08:41.588 --> 08:43.078
I'm sorry, Mr. Aoki.

08:44.557 --> 08:48.152
It's too bad, but I don't think I can keep my promise.

09:11.851 --> 09:13.284
Good job today.

09:13.353 --> 09:14.320
Good job!

09:22.128 --> 09:23.527
Well, I'm off now.

09:23.596 --> 09:26.827
Snack on these waffles while you work overtime.

09:26.900 --> 09:29.061
- Thank you so much!
- See you.

10:18.785 --> 10:21.447
The doors will close on the train on Platform 1.

10:59.759 --> 11:02.421
One problem solved, and another appears...

11:09.836 --> 11:11.326
Hello.

11:11.404 --> 11:14.464
It's been a while, Mr. Seiichiro Aoki.

11:16.509 --> 11:18.568
Oh, hello there.

11:18.645 --> 11:20.078
What a coincidence.

11:21.180 --> 11:23.410
Do you always go home at this time?

11:23.483 --> 11:26.748
No, I just happened to leave early today.

11:27.720 --> 11:30.120
I usually go home pretty late...

11:30.189 --> 11:33.625
...thanks to authors' manuscripts or proofreading.

11:33.693 --> 11:36.753
The publishing industry is rather tough, as well.

11:36.829 --> 11:38.228
Yes.

11:38.297 --> 11:41.460
And apologizing to printers on the artists' behalf...

11:41.534 --> 11:43.832
...for late manuscripts.

11:43.903 --> 11:46.633
I'm never lacking in worrying about others.

11:46.706 --> 11:49.607
I'm rather jealous of government officials.

11:50.643 --> 11:51.769
Is that so?

11:53.046 --> 11:55.776
By the way, where are you headed now?

11:55.848 --> 11:57.713
I can't tell you that.

11:57.784 --> 12:01.447
If I invite you to our base...

12:01.521 --> 12:03.284
...I'll get scolded.

12:04.323 --> 12:05.620
I see...

12:06.659 --> 12:08.957
Things aren't really going well...

12:10.797 --> 12:13.231
I can hang out till I get close.

12:14.267 --> 12:15.393
Please.

12:16.669 --> 12:20.730
I saw how you handled things the other day.

12:20.807 --> 12:23.207
You're pretty powerful.

12:23.276 --> 12:26.837
I have many people that I have to protect.

12:27.847 --> 12:30.008
You're saying you become stronger...

12:30.083 --> 12:32.415
...when you have people you have to protect?

12:32.485 --> 12:33.577
That's right.

12:35.488 --> 12:38.651
That's why I was able to become stronger.

12:38.725 --> 12:39.749
Is that so?

12:40.793 --> 12:43.591
I don't think that's always the case...

12:43.663 --> 12:45.494
After all, what was his name?

12:46.532 --> 12:48.727
The one who died so easily...

12:48.801 --> 12:51.065
...protecting your dreamgazing princess?

12:53.840 --> 12:54.966
Let's begin.

12:56.776 --> 12:57.743
Sure.

13:11.023 --> 13:12.320
A Barrier...

13:14.227 --> 13:15.194
True...

13:16.329 --> 13:19.127
There's no way that Yuto would be late for tea.

13:51.464 --> 13:52.954
Beast, hurry!

13:55.802 --> 13:57.099
Ouch...

13:57.170 --> 14:00.162
Why are you in such a bad mood today?

14:00.239 --> 14:02.332
Please hurry!

14:11.217 --> 14:15.119
Oh no, this coat's no longer good.

14:15.188 --> 14:16.780
It was expensive, too.

14:17.824 --> 14:21.954
Oh, but pretty soon, you won't need a coat anymore.

14:42.882 --> 14:45.578
Oh, that saved me, Satsuki.

14:46.619 --> 14:49.747
Now I think I'll somehow make it in time for tea...

15:05.805 --> 15:10.265
It's a job well done if I can get rid of you for the price of a coat...

15:12.311 --> 15:13.278
Hot...

15:14.780 --> 15:16.645
That's not what you promised!

15:16.716 --> 15:19.651
I thought I told you to ask for me next time!

15:19.719 --> 15:21.516
K-Karen!

15:21.587 --> 15:23.782
There was such a promise, wasn't there?

15:23.856 --> 15:26.017
Then can I ask to change to you?

15:26.092 --> 15:27.218
This one time.

15:32.498 --> 15:33.931
K-Karen!

15:35.034 --> 15:38.231
Beast, back Yuto up one more time.

15:43.109 --> 15:45.771
We ended up like this again...

15:45.845 --> 15:48.439
It can't be helped since we're water and fire...

15:48.514 --> 15:51.244
But why are you so desperate to fight?

15:53.286 --> 15:55.083
Oh, is it him?

15:56.122 --> 15:58.647
Can it be you're in love with Mr. Aoki?

15:59.692 --> 16:01.751
I don't approve.

16:01.827 --> 16:05.092
Mr. Aoki has a wife and child, after all.

16:06.465 --> 16:10.094
Oh, but he seems to have filed for divorce...

16:10.169 --> 16:11.363
...so it's all right.

16:15.508 --> 16:16.907
I'm happy for you.

16:16.976 --> 16:19.536
I don't want anything like that.

16:19.612 --> 16:20.579
Do you know?

16:20.646 --> 16:24.707
If one grain of wheat falls to earth and dies, it will bear much fruit.

16:28.287 --> 16:29.413
What is that?

16:35.027 --> 16:38.519
It's a line from John's Revelations in the Bible.

16:38.597 --> 16:42.089
It means that you're better off sacrificing your life...

16:42.168 --> 16:45.296
...to help the world where your loved ones live.

16:45.371 --> 16:48.568
That's what it means to protect someone dear to you!

16:49.608 --> 16:50.905
Beast!

16:50.977 --> 16:52.638
Why aren't you moving?

16:52.712 --> 16:54.270
Protect Yuto!

17:12.765 --> 17:14.733
Forgive me, my Lord...

17:29.148 --> 17:30.115
Mr. Aoki!

17:32.151 --> 17:33.743
No! Run!

17:34.787 --> 17:37.984
I didn't want to attack a lady from behind...

17:38.991 --> 17:41.391
...but this is payback for burning me.

17:49.502 --> 17:52.471
I don't want to slash your throat...

17:52.538 --> 17:54.335
...so I'll have you drown to death.

17:55.374 --> 17:56.705
It's too bad...

17:57.743 --> 18:00.541
In the end, you couldn't help anyone.

18:02.448 --> 18:04.746
You really are a person worthy of pity...

18:08.821 --> 18:09.845
Huh?

18:09.922 --> 18:11.583
It's too late now.

18:15.361 --> 18:16.658
Karen!

18:19.999 --> 18:20.966
Yuto!

18:21.967 --> 18:23.161
Let go!

18:23.235 --> 18:24.429
Let me go!

18:24.503 --> 18:26.266
I won't ask you anymore!

18:33.379 --> 18:35.711
B-Beast...

18:38.384 --> 18:39.351
Karen!

18:44.790 --> 18:46.223
Karen!

18:46.292 --> 18:47.589
It's me, Aoki!

18:48.627 --> 18:49.594
Karen!

18:52.131 --> 18:53.189
Mr. Aoki...

18:55.234 --> 18:57.998
Are your injuries all right?

18:59.038 --> 19:00.562
Yes.

19:00.639 --> 19:02.072
Thanks to you...

19:03.409 --> 19:05.536
I'm glad...

19:06.278 --> 19:10.647
I can't let a wonderful father like you...

19:12.818 --> 19:14.183
...die.

19:15.221 --> 19:17.451
You're a wonderful woman yourself!

19:18.491 --> 19:19.617
Thank you...

19:22.194 --> 19:29.532
I'm really glad that I was able to protect you...

19:37.009 --> 19:38.601
Karen...

19:51.257 --> 19:52.315
Satsuki...

20:06.539 --> 20:07.665
Satsuki...

20:09.041 --> 20:11.168
The reason we can't kill people...

20:12.978 --> 20:16.846
Is it really because there are people that will be sad?

20:19.218 --> 20:21.584
Oh well, it doesn't matter anymore...

20:23.422 --> 20:26.220
Anyway, tonight's tea party...

20:27.893 --> 20:31.329
I guess I won't be able to make it at all...

20:32.798 --> 20:34.095
It's a shame...
